"all that is needed" is something very difficult to attain.  It
requires, for instance, knowing how much time the average player
spends on each dungeon level.  The longer you spend on a level, the
more monsters (hence potions) will be created.  And you need that
number per-level, since the distribution of intelligent higher level
monsters (who can get the rnd_defensive_item), barracks, shops, and
many other things differ by dungeon level, and certainly the amount of
time I spend on, say, the mines entrance through Sokoban levels is
much higher the the amount I spend on the levels above the mines
entrance level.

But it's impossible to extrapolate from my experience here, anyway,
since there are players who are much more deliberate than I am.
Assuming that the amount of time I spend on a level is close to
average is pretty sketchy without any data.


